tests:
  unit: { count: 15, covers: "The silent-harness guard, both halves. The run tally's judge: all spec files passed is green and says how many; a missing tally (wdio exited without writing one), an unparseable tally, a run configured with no spec file, a failed spec file, and fewer passed spec files than configured (the service failed before any spec started, which leaves wdio green) are each red with a sentence naming it. The static refusals: no ui/e2e spec selects with *= (the embedded WebKit provider never matches it and never errors), no tracked package.json carries a pnpm field (pnpm 10+ ignores it with only an install warning), and ui/e2e/pnpm-workspace.yaml keeps the @wdio/native-utils 2.5.0 override. Each detector is also tested on a fixture, so a green repo check is not merely a detector that finds nothing. The pre-existing ui module tests (usage errors, the window's minimum width) still run beside them." }
  integration: { waived: "W4 adds no bounded contract. The e2e harness is test support, and the gate tool's surface is unchanged: cargo xtask ui e2e keeps its arguments and only refuses a run that passed fewer spec files than it configured, which the unit tests pin. UC-8's contract is already asserted at integration by W1's tests/replay.rs and W3's App.test.tsx." }
  e2e: { count: 35, covers: "THE EPIC'S E2E, through the real Tauri window against a real ephemeral core and the harness's local TLS origin, green under cargo xtask ui e2e: 4 of 4 spec files, 43 tests (onboarding 8, capture 3, replay 6, flows 26). replay.spec.ts drives the three journeys the epic plan named. Replay with one edit: a proxied request to the origin's /echo carrying x-probe: original is opened, replay opens the composer, the x-probe value (found by its name field, since two rows may share a name) is changed and it is the only row marked edited; send disables with sending... beside it for the origin's two-second pause; the 200 pill, a duration and open the new flow land; the list's top row wears the sent mark; and the new flow's raw response body, which is the headers the origin received, carries \"x-probe\":\"edited\" - the edit asserted on the wire, not on the flow. Compose from scratch: new request has an empty URL and a disabled send reading a request needs a URL; with the echo URL it sends and lands; the URL is still there afterwards and still takes typing. A send that fails: the URL set to a port the harness bound and released, send yields the send-failed line with the warning glyph and the core's connection-refused sentence, no element in the send zone named by a number (so no pill and no duration), and the row count unchanged. The spec leaves the capture empty, as capture.spec.ts before it does, so flows.spec.ts starts where it always has. capture.spec.ts and flows.spec.ts each had one selector W3's markup made stale (the paste box's textarea now sits inside Field's span; the flow line's first button is now replay, not copy as curl) - found by this WU's first run, fixed to select what the product renders, the assertions unchanged." }
